    {
      "id": "delivery-workflow",
      "title": "Consent-gated delivery workflow",
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 900,
      "subtitle": "IMPLEMENTED WORKFLOW RULES: issue-linked branches, explicit shipping consent, and safe return to main.",
      "description": "Work starts on an MP issue branch, runs applicable gates, and asks before creating a PR. The exact head must pass CI. Explicit consent precedes merging and closure of the verified completed Jira issue, then a clean local checkout returns to main. Independent review is optional and each round requires approval. If Jira closure fails, still attempt the safe local return and report both outcomes separately.",
      "note": "Optional independent review: ask first; fresh parallel lanes; delta follow-ups; separate consent per round.",
      "footer": "CI is configured; server-side branch protection is inactive under the current GitHub plan. No auto-deploy.",
